@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy policy";
}
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
<h2>Privacy policy (Prototype version)</h2>

<p>This application, Bindicator, has been developed as a prototype for academic and demonstration purposes. No real user data is collected, processed, or stored by the application.</p>

<p><strong>Data Collection:</strong> Only simulated IoT sensor data related to bin fill levels, weights, environmental readings, and locations is processed. This data is either generated artificially or transmitted from non-identifiable sources. No personal data or personally identifiable information (PII) is used or stored.</p>

<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> The application demonstrates the functionality of a smart waste management system, including sensor data visualisation, predictive analytics, and route optimisation. It is not intended for live deployment or use by the public.</p>

<p><strong>Security:</strong> All reasonable precautions have been taken to protect the simulated data, including secure database access and use of encrypted communication channels where appropriate.</p>

<p><strong>Contact:</strong> For any queries about the prototype or its operation, please contact the development team.</p>

<p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> This prototype is not connected to any real-world waste collection services, and any decisions made based on the application outputs are for demonstration purposes only.</p>

<h2>Privacy policy (Production version)</h2>

<p>Your privacy is important to us. This Privacy Policy explains how Bindicator collects, uses, discloses, and protects your information when you use our services.</p>

<h3>1. Information We Collect</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Sensor Data:</strong> We collect data from smart bin sensors, including fill levels, weight, temperature, humidity, bin location (postcode, street name, coordinates), and timestamps.</li>
    <li><strong>User Data:</strong> If applicable, we may collect user account information such as name, email address, and service preferences when you interact with the application.</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. How We Use Your Information</h3>
<ul>
    <li>To provide real-time monitoring of bin statuses and environmental conditions.</li>
    <li>To predict bin fill levels and optimise collection routes.</li>
    <li>To improve operational efficiency and reduce environmental impact.</li>
    <li>To respond to user queries or support requests if you contact us.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Data Sharing and Disclosure</h3>
<p>We do not sell or rent your information to third parties. Data may be shared with authorised service providers (such as cloud hosting providers) solely for the purposes of running and maintaining the system.</p>

<h3>4. Security Measures</h3>
<p>We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to safeguard the data we collect, including data encryption, access controls, and secure communications protocols.</p>

<h3>5. Data Retention</h3>
<p>Sensor and user data will be retained only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes outlined in this Privacy Policy unless a longer retention period is required by law.</p>

<h3>6. Your Rights</h3>
<ul>
    <li>You have the right to access, correct, or delete your personal data.</li>
    <li>You may also request restrictions on the processing of your data or object to certain types of processing.</li>
</ul>

<h3>7. Contact Us</h3>
<p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise your rights, please contact us at <a href="mailto:BindicatorSupport@email.com">BindicatorSupport@email.com</a>.</p>

<h3>8. Changes to this Policy</h3>
<p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any significant changes will be notified to users appropriately.</p>
